   "title": "M2.5 · BPF",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "M2.5: BPF (break-point function / automation curve), drawn in the node.\n\nBPF (draw here), top left: the curve editor.\n- click empty space: add a point (keep the button down to drag it)\n- drag a point: move it (Shift: snap to the grid, Alt: value only)\n- double-click or right-click a point, or select it and press Delete: remove it\n- hover: the point's time and value; elsewhere, the curve's value under the cursor\nduration_ms, min and max set the box; interpolation (step / linear / exp) redraws at once.\n\nPress Run. Look at:\n1. \"Rescaled 200–8000, resampled every 250 ms\": a BPF node with a BPF on its input shows that curve read-only (green) and passes it on: your drawing mapped from 0–1 to 200–8000 and sampled every 250 ms (17 points).\n2. \"Loaded from file\": input/m5_swell.bpf.json (Load BPF) shown the same way. \"Edit a copy\" copies it into the editor and disconnects the input.\n\nSave and reopen the workflow: the drawn points are kept."
   ],
